  <main_text>
    <l n="1">rat, adducitur aliquando id fulmen: &amp;</l>
    <l n="2">vicissim campanarum pulsu avertitur,</l>
    <l n="3">non quidem ita, ut non sint contraria</l>
    <l n="4">exempla tactæ hujusmodi turris, sed</l>
    <l n="5">tantum sæpe sic libera præstatur.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">§. 4. Respectu virtutis fulmen in <i>te-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>rebrans</i>, <i>dissipans</i>, &amp; <i>urens</i> dispescitur.</l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Terebrans</i> etiam minutissima transit ob</l>
    <l n="9">virtutem potentem in subtili spiritu</l>
    <l n="10">fundatam:<i>dissipans</i> autem ob materiam</l>
    <l n="11">terrestriorem disjicit, &amp; dirumpit ob-</l>
    <l n="12">stantia, at non ita urit: <i>Vrens</i> autem</l>
    <l n="13">omnia in flammam conjicit ob multum</l>
    <l n="14">sulphur tenax adjunctum. Vlterius au-</l>
    <l n="15">tem notantur varii fulminum mirabi-</l>
    <l n="16">les effectus: ut quod loculo illæso ar-</l>
    <l n="17">gentum, vagina non fracta ferrum eli-</l>
    <l n="18">quarit: quod vestimentis &amp; cute illæsis</l>
    <l n="19">ossa contriverit,dolio illæso vinum cor-</l>
    <l n="20">ruperit, &amp;c.: Hæc &amp; similia judicem</l>
    <l n="21">pendere à materia valde tenui, quæ per</l>
    <l n="22">quæcunque exigua transire potest, &amp;</l>
    <l n="23">tamen magnas virtutes in contrariis &amp;</l>
    <l n="24">obstaculis exercet. Observatum etiam</l>
    <l n="25">est fulmina aliquando dolio confracto</l>
    <l n="26">vinum quasi stabile reddidisse. Hoc à</l>
    <l n="27">crassiore materia &amp; figente sulphurea</l>
    <l n="28">provenire censeo. Atque huc retulerim</l>
    <l n="29">quoque, quod ex Cardano Fromond.I.</l>
